                    {
                        "sense_id": "ecbb5231-c2ab-3ef6-91c8-117d461a5f5a",
                        "entry_id": "755a9349-a943-3305-8231-35aad9849e39",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Relating to distribution."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d5dc0bfc-07e5-37e7-be37-818de9071287",
                        "entry_id": "755a9349-a943-3305-8231-35aad9849e39",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Tending to distribute; serving to divide and assign in portions; dealing a proper share to each."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8786b327-8e22-486b-b15e-3087180cb6ef",
                                "sense_id": "d5dc0bfc-07e5-37e7-be37-818de9071287",
                                "text": "[I]t is worth obſerving the diſtributive Juſtice of the Authors, which is conſtantly applied to the Puniſhment of Virtue, and the Reward of Vice; […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a58e5652-1ef0-39b7-8bac-7947757ad68a",
                        "entry_id": "755a9349-a943-3305-8231-35aad9849e39",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A property of functions that have a rule describing how the function can be performed to the individual components of another operation."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "96e911b9-d679-49f7-9ca1-1b11fdeceef1",
                                "sense_id": "a58e5652-1ef0-39b7-8bac-7947757ad68a",
                                "text": "If function f is distributive with respect to function g, then f(a,g(b,c))=g(f(a,b),f(a,c))."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "573f34aa-5a6a-482b-aee5-98b4c9f9ae02",
                                "sense_id": "a58e5652-1ef0-39b7-8bac-7947757ad68a",
                                "text": "If the operation ⋆ is distributive with respect to the operation ∘, then a⋆(b∘c)=(a⋆b)∘(a⋆c)."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "eeed4d98-7bcb-35ed-b7d3-8284e8c6d6f7",
                        "entry_id": "755a9349-a943-3305-8231-35aad9849e39",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Assigning the species of a general term."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "478f0ad9-f929-3142-97cd-a97d36778679",
                        "entry_id": "755a9349-a943-3305-8231-35aad9849e39",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Expressing separation; denoting a taking singly, not collectively."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c3de7f3a-2b10-4cb7-bdbd-1ce0e8df7651",
                                "sense_id": "478f0ad9-f929-3142-97cd-a97d36778679",
                                "text": "a distributive adjective or pronoun, such as \"each\", \"either\", or \"every\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "492dd68d-1f47-428c-a004-242ed59d9590",
                                "sense_id": "478f0ad9-f929-3142-97cd-a97d36778679",
                                "text": "a distributive numeral, such as Latin \"bini\" (two by two)"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
